==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|mono|cotyledon}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌmɒnəˌkɒtɪˈliːdən/}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} Any plant whose seedlings typically have one [[cotyledon]] ([[seed leaf]]) (in contrast to the two cotyledons typical of [[dicot]]s), thereby belonging to the taxonomic [[monocots]], formerly variously known as {{taxlink|Monocotyledones|class|noshow=1}}, {{taxlink|Monocotyledonae|class|noshow=1}}, or [[Liliopsida]], a class in the [[angiosperms]] ([[Angiospermae]]), the [[flowering plant]]s.

====Usage notes====
* Outside definitions or strict taxonomic usage, {{m|en|monocot}} is the preferred form.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|plant with single seed leaf}} {{l|en|monocot}}, {{l|en|liliopsid}}

====Hyponyms====
* {{sense|plant with single seed leaf}} [[grass]], [[lily]], [[orchid]], [[palm]]

